      "title": "Suspected mass bird flu deaths found in second state as Murray Watt warns ‘this is the beginning’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/03/suspected-mass-bird-flu-deaths-found-in-second-state-as-murray-watt-warns-this-is-the-beginning",
      "description": "<p>Environment minister says Australia has ‘long and difficult journey’ and says more mass mortality events likely</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Aerial surveillance has detected mass bird deaths in a second Australian state in another suspected escalation of the spread of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/bird-flu\">deadly H5 bird flu</a>.</p><p>The environment minister, Murray Watt, said on Monday Australia had begun “a long and difficult journey” as CSIRO analysis confirmed Australia’s first mass mortality event at <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/01/first-australian-mass-mortality-event-suspected-as-deadly-bird-flu-virus-rapidly-escalates-among-native-birds\">Baudin Rocks</a> off South Australia’s coast.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/03/suspected-mass-bird-flu-deaths-found-in-second-state-as-murray-watt-warns-this-is-the-beginning\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-03T10:27:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Teenager didn’t tell anyone Alan Jones allegedly kissed and touched him as he feared losing financial help, trial hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/03/alan-jones-trial-update-sydney-court-case-day-1-news-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Former 2UE and 2GB radio broadcaster is facing 22 charges. Jones, 85, has pleaded not guilty</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/03/alan-jones-trial-live-updates-indecent-assault-charges-day-1-sydney-court-case-latest-news-ntwnfb\">Alan Jones trial day one – as it happened</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li><li><p><em>Warning: may contain graphic content</em></p></li></ul><p>A former schoolboy athlete has told the Alan Jones trial he didn’t tell anyone the broadcaster was allegedly kissing him and touching his genitalia when he was a teenager because he was “fearful” of losing Jones’s financial support.</p><p>The man, known as complainant J, alleged that after he drove Jones to a function in Canberra and they were alone in the hotel room, Jones kissed him in a “smothering” way. After the drive back to Sydney, Jones allegedly said to him: “You’ve been a really good boy. I’m going to give you some more money.” His regular weekly stipend increased by $100, the court heard. J also said Jones told him he didn’t have to tell anyone he was giving him money as it was “a gift”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/03/alan-jones-trial-update-sydney-court-case-day-1-news-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-03T08:16:43"
    },
    {
      "title": "Greens senator brands Pauline Hanson a ‘political coward’ over press conference bans – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/03/australia-news-live-fuel-excise-cut-jim-chalmers-cost-of-living-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed</p><p><strong>Angus Taylor and Anthony Albanese on leave this week</strong></p><p>The opposition leader, <strong>Angus Taylor,</strong> is on leave for most of this week, his office has announced, with the deputy leader, <strong>Jane Hume,</strong> acting in his stead.</p><p>NSWRL owes a massive debt of gratitude to Laurie for the service he has given to his state as both a player and a coach.</p><p>He has also led NSW to arguably two of the greatest Origin series wins of all time as a coach, after ending Queensland’s eight-year winning streak in 2014 and overcoming adversity to steer the Blues home in 2026.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/03/australia-news-live-fuel-excise-cut-jim-chalmers-cost-of-living-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
